        <body>
            
            <div type="edition" xml:lang="tam-Latn" rendition="class:vaṭṭeḻuttu maturity:83215">
                
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/>
                    <hi rend="grantha">śrī</hi>
                </ab>
                
                <p>
                    kō-vicaiya-para<unclear>mēc</unclear>cuvara-parumaṟku
                    <lb n="2"/>yāṇṭu Oṉpat-āvatu
                </p>
                
                <p>			
                    <unclear>va</unclear>miṟaiyār vē
                    <lb n="3" break="no"/>ṇāṭ-iḷa-k-kōvūr-nāṭṭu kō<choice><orig>-I</orig><reg>yi</reg></choice>l paṭṭar van
                    <lb n="4" break="no"/>tu toṟu-k koṇṭa nāṉṟu mēṟ-ceṅkai māmm-u
                    <lb n="5" break="no"/>ṭaiya pāra
                    <lb n="6" break="no"/>tāyar maka
                    <lb n="7" break="no"/>ṉ toṟu mī
                    <lb n="8" break="no"/>ṭṭu-p <supplied reason="lost">paṭṭā</supplied>
                    <lb n="9" break="no"/>ṉ mukaṉ	
                </p>
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="apparatus">
                
                <listApp>
                    <app loc="8">
                        <lem><supplied reason="lost">paṭṭā</supplied>
                            <lb n="9" break="no"/>ṉ</lem>
                        <rdg source="bib:Nakacami1972_01"><gap reason="lost" quantity="2" unit="character" precision="low"/>
                            <lb n="9" break="no"/>ṉ</rdg>         			
                    </app>      		
                    
                </listApp>
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
                
                <p n="1">
                    <supplied reason="lost">Fortune!</supplied>
                </p>
                
                <p n="1-2">
                    Ninth year of the victorious king Paramēccuvaraparumaṉ.<note>Sanskrit Parameśvaravarman.</note>
                </p>
                
                <p n="3-8">
                    Mukaṉ<!--Update:add markup for translation unclear, tentative-->, the son <supplied reason="subaudible">of</supplied> Pāratāyar, the lord of Mēṟceṅkai<note>Alternatively, simply "Pāratāyar of Mēṟceṅkai".</note><!--Update: translate: māmm. Part of the placename-->, fell recovering cattle, when <supplied reason="lost">Va</supplied>miṟaiyār<!--Update:add markup for translation unclear, tentative-->, a temple dignitary <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>kōyil paṭṭar</foreign></supplied> in Iḷakkōvūrnāṭu in Vēṇāṭu, came and seized cattle.
                    
                </p>      		
                
            </div>
            
